CloudBurrow patch 25 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1204). Applies after patch 0021.

The bug: UNNEST of an array holding an infinite FLOAT64, such as
SELECT x FROM UNNEST([CAST('inf' AS FLOAT64)]) AS x, failed "failed to scan
rows: json: unsupported value: +Inf". UNNEST reads the array through
json_each(googlesqlite_decode_array(...)), and googlesqlite_decode_array
wrote each element's EncodeValue, a bare float64 for a FLOAT64, into JSON,
which has no infinity. Patch 0004 already puts an infinity inside an ARRAY or
a STRUCT in the value envelope (encodeElement); the patch exports that as
value.EncodeElement and uses it in googlesqlite_decode_array, so the element
reaches json_each as the envelope and is read back as the infinity. BigQuery
returns the row, Infinity. inf_unnest_test.go fails without the patch and
passes with it.

